/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In the bridge of Network terminology, the 10 Ω arm from B to C joins the two halves.
   - The replacement is equivalent at the three terminals only: the same terminal voltages give the same terminal currents, and the total power entering the group is the same.
   - Call the delta resistors RAB, RBC and RCA, and the star arms RA, RB, RC from the centre N to the terminals.
   - RA = RABRCA/S, RB = RABRBC/S, RC = RBCRCA/S, where S = RAB + RBC + RCA.
   - Memory rule: star arm = product of the two delta sides that touch that terminal ÷ sum of all three.
   - Going back, let P = RARB + RBRC + RCRA (the sum of the products taken two at a time).
   - Balanced case: when all three resistors are equal, RY = RΔ/3 and RΔ = 3RY; for example 30 Ω delta sides become 10 Ω star arms.
*/
