/* book Worked example: Q: A delta has RAB = 10 Ω, RBC = 20 Ω and RCA = 30 Ω. Find the equivalent star and convert it back as a check.
   1. S = 10 + 20 + 30 = 60 Ω.
   2. RA = RABRCA/S = 10 × 30/60 = 5 Ω; RB = RABRBC/S = 10 × 20/60 = 3.333 Ω; RC = RBCRCA/S = 20 × 30/60 = 10 Ω.
   3. Check back: P = 5 × 3.333 + 3.333 × 10 + 10 × 5 = 16.667 + 33.333 + 50 = 100 Ω².
   4. RAB = P/RC = 100/10 = 10 Ω; RBC = P/RA = 100/5 = 20 Ω; RCA = P/RB = 100/3.333 = 30 Ω. The delta returns.
   Answer: RA = 5 Ω, RB = 10/3 ≈ 3.333 Ω, RC = 10 Ω. */
